1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,641
Eat it with the soup.
It's better that way.

3
00:00:58,642 --> 00:01:00,185
I'll eat however I want to.

4
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:03,397
- It tastes better this way.
- Come on.

5
00:01:04,273 --> 00:01:06,066
Just trust me and try it.

6
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:10,695
I like the original taste
of tuna rice balls.

7
00:01:10,696 --> 00:01:12,238
Original taste, my foot.

8
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:14,115
This is how you enjoy
tteokbokki stew.

9
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:16,034
I can just add soup
to the fried rice later.

10
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:18,244
Fried rice should be eaten on its own

11
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:19,955
so the scorched rice stays crispy.

12
00:01:20,372 --> 00:01:22,707
We just can't seem to see eye to eye.

13
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:24,042
- Get more pickled radish.
- Yes, ma'am.

14
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:28,589
Here you go.

15
00:01:29,298 --> 00:01:30,299
Another drink?

16
00:01:35,304 --> 00:01:36,305
Look, it's Yoo Ji-hyun.

17
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:41,727
I reviewed her contract
for the Laknes ad.

18
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,187
Just because of that,
I feel closer to her now.

19
00:01:44,563 --> 00:01:46,897
Same here. Now that she's
in our company's ad

20
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,734
- I like her more.
- Right?

21
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:52,278
I feel bad for her.

22
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:53,696
Why did she have to get a divorce?

23
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,991
She lost her family,
and she'll lose her model pay.

24
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,327
Why would she lose her pay?

25
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,455
In cases like this,
the contract is usually terminated.

26
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:03,332
The ad hasn't gone public yet

27
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:06,585
so there's no need for the company
to use someone in a controversy.

28
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:20,432
EPISODE 6: PROBLEM RECOGNIZES PROBLEM

29
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:25,604
All right.

30
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,066
Is it hazelnut?

31
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:31,400
Of course.

32
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:32,402
You haven't forgotten.

33
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:34,905
How could I forget
your preference, Mr. Son?

34
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:39,785
So why did you want to see me?

35
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,161
What do you mean?

36
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,037
I just wanted to enjoy

37
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:45,790
a cup of coffee with you
since it's been a while.

38
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:46,917
Bullshit.

39
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:51,922
Well, it's about contract workers.

40
00:02:52,381 --> 00:02:53,382
What about them?

41
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:56,884
Team 2's contract worker
seems to be doing a great job.

42
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:58,553
Yeah, he's fantastic.

43
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:00,847
Since he's doing well

44
00:03:01,515 --> 00:03:03,349
you probably won't
have to worry about him.

45
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:08,271
Could you keep an eye out
for Lee Ji-hye of Team 5?

46
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:15,946
Hey.

47
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:18,824
Do you know
what your reputation at work is?

48
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,201
- My reputation?
- Yeah.

49
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,160
How is it?

50
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,287
It's good.

51
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:26,372
Some even call you an ace.

52
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:28,416
Gosh, that's all thanks
to what you taught me...

53
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:32,129
But why do you think
you're still an assistant manager?

54
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:37,968
If you tell me now,
I'll take it to heart.

55
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,804
You're a good problem solver.

56
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:42,514
The problem with that is

57
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,433
you only solve the internal issues.

58
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:46,559
Demands from higher-ups

59
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,227
conflicts among the juniors

60
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,896
and office politics, stuff like that.

61
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:54,358
So whether or not you can solve
a real issue at the company

62
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,610
remains to be seen.

63
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:00,156
I'm telling you this
because I care about you.

64
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:01,158
Don't be upset, okay?

65
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,077
Oh, I'm not upset at all.

66
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:08,372
Stop focusing on things
like the contract workers

67
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:09,750
and do some real work.

68
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,168
That will benefit you.

69
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:12,961
Yes, sir.

70
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,217
Hang on.

71
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,595
You call your team's
contract worker by her name

72
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:23,680
but the one in my team
is just a "contract worker"?

73
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,558
You don't even know his name

74
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:29,060
but ask me to keep
an eye out for Ji-hye?

75
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,396
Yoon Jeong-min.

76
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:33,690
That's his name.

77
00:04:34,608 --> 00:04:35,609
Got it.

78
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:39,279
- One moment.
- Sure.

79
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:43,909
Yes, hello?

80
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:46,578
Yes.

81
00:04:48,038 --> 00:04:49,039
Sorry?

82
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,425
- Hello, Mr. Gong.
- Hello, Mr. Yang.

83
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,259
Where's Gi-tae?

84
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,471
He hasn't come in yet.

85
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,899
INCOMING CALL
MR. YANG JUN-HO

86
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,901
Yes, I understand.

87
00:05:18,902 --> 00:05:20,820
I apologize.
We should've handled it sooner.

88
00:05:20,821 --> 00:05:21,988
All right, goodbye.

89
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,450
The Distribution Team
must be in chaos.

90
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:28,577
Their schedule is screwed up,
so they're very upset.

91
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:29,830
Is Gi-tae still not picking up?

92
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,498
No, he's not.

93
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:35,126
He's not the type to run away
from his own mess.

94
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:38,839
Let's figure out how to fix this.

95
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:41,215
This is the current situation.

96
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:43,425
We placed an additional order
for 300 million won

97
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,928
but the purchase order said
three billion won by mistake.

98
00:05:45,929 --> 00:05:48,472
Laknes followed the purchase order
and sent the goods

99
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:50,517
which just arrived in Incheon.

100
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:53,812
But didn't Laknes reach out?

101
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:57,232
Surely, they would've known
there was an issue with the quantity.

102
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:59,025
We don't know that.

103
00:05:59,276 --> 00:06:01,026
Let's not jump to conclusions.

104
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:03,028
Even 300 million was
a generous order.

105
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:05,615
We won't be able to handle
three billion.

106
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:08,118
If we go by retail price,
isn't that over ten billion?

107
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:09,910
That is the problem.

108
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,037
How should we solve it?

109
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,417
We'll start with
what Gi-tae didn't do.

110
00:06:16,418 --> 00:06:17,794
I'll report it to Mr. Jang.

111
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:20,462
Ms. Jang, you'll come with me.

112
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,881
Mr. Yang and Ji-hye.

113
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:24,551
- Find Gi-tae and bring him to me.
- Yes, sir.

114
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,094
Mr. Gong.

115
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,430
May I come with you
to see Mr. Jang instead?

116
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:35,562
Well, I asked you to find Gi-tae
because you two are close.

117
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:38,564
We are close,
but this time, I'd like to...

118
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:39,857
I'll go, then.

119
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:40,942
I don't mind.

120
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,614
All right, then.

121
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:47,157
Okay.

122
00:06:50,911 --> 00:06:51,912
Is he in?

123
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:53,455
Yes.

124
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:57,709
Come in.

125
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:05,634
Where's Park Gi-tae?

126
00:07:06,468 --> 00:07:07,802
We're looking for him right now.

127
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:11,889
Aren't purchase orders
under your purview?

128
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:13,058
Didn't you check it?

129
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,061
The first draft was for 250 million.

130
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:19,314
After checking,
I revised it to 300 million.

131
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,191
I failed to check it properly
after that.

132
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:23,193
Are you proud of yourself?

133
00:07:24,736 --> 00:07:25,862
I'm sorry, sir.

134
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:30,283
Did you forget Ms. Park told you
to report to her about every payment?

135
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,789
You reported to me,
so your job is done.

136
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,540
But what about me?

137
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:40,335
Do I need to report this?

138
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:45,715
If you just give us three days,
I think we can fix this.

139
00:07:45,966 --> 00:07:47,300
As for getting the numbers in order

140
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:50,428
I think we can get it done
before the quarterly report.

141
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:56,392
Saying you can do it
and saying you "think" you can do it

142
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,102
are completely different things.

143
00:07:58,103 --> 00:07:59,562
Give it to me straight.

144
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,563
I think we can do it.

145
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:02,565
Damn it.

146
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:07,404
Give it a shot, then.

147
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,948
You have three days
before I report this.

148
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:14,493
Whether I report it
as a minor issue or a disaster

149
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,121
is up to you two.

150
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:17,872
Yes, sir.

151
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:25,587
Did Jang Hyang-eun go to find Gi-tae?

152
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,589
Not you?

153
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:28,549
Yes, sir.

154
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:29,968
Lee Ji-hye went with her.

155
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:31,635
Why are you acting out of character?

156
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,054
Just stick to what you usually do.

157
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:38,560
Just fix this problem first.

158
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:41,021
And bring Park Gi-tae back alive.

159
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:42,521
Yes, sir.

160
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:43,690
Do you have a plan?

161
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:49,862
I think so.

162
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:51,031
Why, you little...

163
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:06,463
Feel free to rest your eyes.

164
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,590
No, I'm all right.

165
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:10,591
Just take it easy.

166
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:11,760
Do I make you uncomfortable?

167
00:09:12,135 --> 00:09:14,137
No, not at all.

168
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:17,599
I just want to be polite.

169
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,643
Being comfortable doesn't mean
you'll start being rude.

170
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:22,604
Right.

171
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:29,569
How was your time in China?

172
00:09:31,613 --> 00:09:32,864
It was boring.

173
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:35,324
For most employees assigned overseas

174
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:37,869
the men run wild,
while the women get bored.

175
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,288
All I did was work.

176
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,626
I see.

177
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:46,920
Is that why you came back?

178
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,299
Haven't you heard
the rumors about me?

179
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:53,885
What rumors?

180
00:09:54,469 --> 00:09:56,720
That I fled after engaging
in corruption in China.

181
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:59,515
That I slept with a top executive,
so I got off easy.

182
00:09:59,516 --> 00:10:01,517
That I'm dating someone
from another team.

183
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:03,519
That all my clothes are knockoffs.

184
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,437
That I'm always at
the counterfeit market in Dongdaemun.

185
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:07,232
That I make 4 million
and spend 5 million on clothes.

186
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:09,150
Those are the ones I've heard.

187
00:10:09,901 --> 00:10:11,444
Haven't you heard any of them?

188
00:10:12,112 --> 00:10:14,906
No, I haven't heard a single one.

189
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:20,245
I've only heard that
you're one of the best employees.

190
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:24,332
If it weren't for our team,
I probably would've quit.

191
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,333
If I were on another team

192
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:29,336
they would've pestered me
about if the rumors were true

193
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,839
and about what happened in China.

194
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:35,218
Shouldn't you say something
instead of toughing it out?

195
00:10:36,219 --> 00:10:37,595
I want to do something.

196
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:40,265
But I don't know what to do.

197
00:10:41,266 --> 00:10:44,102
It's hard to explain myself
when people talk behind my back.

198
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:47,689
In the end,
they'll either believe me or not.

199
00:10:48,231 --> 00:10:50,358
I just have to hope
more people believe me.

200
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,284
Do you think Laknes
really didn't know it was an error?

201
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:02,662
There's no way they didn't know.

202
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:05,832
I know we're the ones who messed up

203
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,876
but it's still really annoying.

204
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,543
Well, what can we do?

205
00:11:09,544 --> 00:11:12,088
Make one mistake,
and this world will rip you apart.

206
00:11:13,131 --> 00:11:17,218
If we take the simple approach,
we just need more retailers.

207
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:20,513
It's not like a retailer
will just fall into our laps.

208
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,683
I actually know of one.

209
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,853
So Mr. Gong.

210
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,607
We need to make sure
the extra stock looks intentional.

211
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,248
Hello, Mr. Gong.

212
00:11:47,582 --> 00:11:48,875
Hello, Mr. Kim.

213
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:53,003
I checked after your sudden request
for a conference call

214
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:55,006
and saw that the additional order
was quite large.

215
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,926
Yes, we would've appreciated it
if you had checked it sooner.

216
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:00,053
It really is a shame.

217
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:02,638
I believe
the person in charge thought

218
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,890
it was a regular order,
not an additional order.

219
00:12:04,891 --> 00:12:08,644
Yes, since it's been two months
since our regular purchase order

220
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:11,855
they must have assumed
the next order was sent early.

221
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:14,858
Right. Well, although
this wasn't our mistake

222
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,778
let's try figuring it out together.

223
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,155
The thing is

224
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:21,157
it wasn't a mistake.

225
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,911
What other retailer do we have?

226
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,746
Our multi-brand store.

227
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:30,999
It wasn't a mistake, you say?

228
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,211
Could you please elaborate?

229
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:36,088
The decision was made on short notice

230
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,674
so we couldn't notify you.

231
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,050
We're launching
a multi-brand shoe store

232
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:41,970
and we want to include Laknes.

233
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,305
I see.

234
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:48,476
So that's the reason you made
such a large order?

235
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:52,271
Yes, we were going to send the order
after negotiating the invoice price

236
00:12:52,272 --> 00:12:53,481
but there was an oversight.

237
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,817
You want to renegotiate the price?

238
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:59,361
The order quantity has
increased significantly

239
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:00,989
so the price should be changed
to reflect that.

240
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:03,574
By how much?

241
00:13:04,826 --> 00:13:06,035
Enough for a justification.

242
00:13:06,703 --> 00:13:09,079
The truth is, there's some opposition

243
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,789
to Laknes joining
the multi-brand store.

244
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,582
There's also opposition
from other brands

245
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:16,045
about selling Laknes' shoes
alongside theirs.

246
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:19,799
We sincerely apologize
for doing things out of order

247
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:23,886
but we hope Laknes can provide us
with a justification.

248
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:27,056
What is the scale
of this multi-brand store?

249
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:30,267
We'll be opening 40 locations
simultaneously.

250
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:31,394
Forty...

251
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:38,151
What if we lower the cost

252
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,362
of additional orders
to two billion won?

253
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:46,908
That price seems reasonable.

254
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,827
That should be enough justification.

255
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,913
But for this one order

256
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:53,458
would you be able to lower it
to 1.5 billion?

257
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:55,960
To 1.5 billion?

258
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:57,586
Will that work?

259
00:13:57,587 --> 00:14:00,213
If they processed the order
knowing it was an error

260
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:01,924
they might feel somewhat guilty.

261
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:03,968
Then it just might work.

262
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:06,137
Yes.

263
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,929
This multi-brand shoe store

264
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:10,599
is a project that will mobilize
company-wide resources.

265
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,727
If Laknes agrees to help out

266
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:15,396
it'll be a huge boost for us.

267
00:14:16,314 --> 00:14:17,523
And this agreement can serve

268
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:20,610
as a reminder to avoid
any future mistakes.

269
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:42,715
Very well.

270
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:44,550
We'll agree to those terms.

271
00:14:48,221 --> 00:14:49,222
Thank you.

272
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,516
No, thank you.
This is a good opportunity for us.

273
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:54,601
I hope it is successful.

274
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:57,521
Also, if it's all right with you

275
00:14:57,522 --> 00:15:01,066
we'd like to include Laknes-branded
shopping bags at the store.

276
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:02,610
It will help promote the brand.

277
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:04,820
Well, sure.

278
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:07,490
Then we'll proceed
and wait for you to send them.

279
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,700
- Thank you.
- All right.

280
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:12,745
THE MEETING HAS ENDED

281
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:16,624
The collective cost of shopping bags
can be around ten million won.

282
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:19,877
What is it?

283
00:15:20,378 --> 00:15:21,379
You were awesome.

284
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:32,140
Do you really think that order
was for the multi-brand store?

285
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:37,061
Come on, we both know
there is no way that's true.

286
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:50,992
Sir!

287
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:54,203
Here, I got the documents.

288
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:57,039
You got this from the Port Authority?

289
00:15:57,331 --> 00:15:58,332
Yes, sir.

290
00:15:58,583 --> 00:15:59,584
Well...

291
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,002
REPORT OF PORT CARGO HANDLING RATES
AND CHARGES

292
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:03,336
Did they allow this?

293
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:05,882
This provides two extra weeks
of storage free of charge.

294
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,134
Everything's good now, right?

295
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,051
All right, then.

296
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:11,511
You have two weeks.

297
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:12,972
After that, it's not my concern.

298
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:16,350
Thank you so much, sir.

299
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:19,436
Wait, don't forget your phone.

300
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:20,480
It's been ringing all day.

301
00:16:20,855 --> 00:16:22,148
Oh, right.

302
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,403
17 MISSED CALLS FROM
MR. YANG JUN-HO

303
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,616
- Thank you.
- Sure.

304
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,413
Ji-hye.

305
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:38,831
Ms. Jang.

306
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:50,009
So tell me.

307
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:52,803
Were you going to report back
after trying to fix it?

308
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,974
Yes, I figured
that's the least I could do.

309
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:02,145
What will happen to us now?

310
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:03,189
Why?

311
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:05,900
Do you think you'll get fired
over this one mistake?

312
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:08,528
Well, my getting fired
doesn't matter.

313
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:11,280
But won't this affect
our team's results?

314
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:15,535
It won't be good for Ji-hye, either.

315
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:20,206
Gi-tae, don't think like that.

316
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:28,089
Mr. Gong told me to relay a message
when we found you, Gi-tae.

317
00:17:28,923 --> 00:17:29,966
Ms. Jang.

318
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:31,508
Yes, sir.

319
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:33,718
Check out the Port Authority
or the container terminal.

320
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:37,098
Gi-tae isn't the type to hide away
and drink over his mistakes.

321
00:17:37,807 --> 00:17:40,101
- Yes, sir.
- And give him this message for me.

322
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:45,314
This incident was my fault.

323
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:48,066
So I'll be the one
to take accountability.

324
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,569
"This incident was my fault.

325
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,113
So I'll be the one
to take accountability.

326
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:54,448
Don't be cheeky
and try to take the blame yourself."

327
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:56,325
Those were his words.

328
00:17:58,744 --> 00:18:00,829
That doesn't sound like Mr. Gong.

329
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:02,081
The sentiment is the same.

330
00:18:06,294 --> 00:18:08,671
Didn't you think about
how upset Mr. Gong would be?

331
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:10,672
Because I messed up?

332
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:12,383
No, because you didn't tell him.

333
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,634
As soon as Mr. Gong found out

334
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:17,095
the first thing he did
was report to Mr. Jang.

335
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,848
Because he trusts Mr. Jang.

336
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,016
You treated Mr. Gong like someone

337
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,103
who evades responsibility
and can't solve problems.

338
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:28,482
Is that what he thinks?

339
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:30,901
Probably not.

340
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:32,987
Right.

341
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:36,073
Everyone makes mistakes at work.

342
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:39,577
So don't make a big deal of it.
Got it?

343
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:41,912
Does everyone make mistakes

344
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:43,997
this big?

345
00:18:43,998 --> 00:18:45,041
Rarely.

346
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:47,835
Right.

347
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:04,268
AD MODEL CONTRACT

348
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:10,273
How fast do you need it?

349
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:12,734
He's on his way to her
with the contract

350
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:14,653
so we'll need it within the hour.

351
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:16,364
He already left with the contract?

352
00:19:17,448 --> 00:19:18,532
Are you kidding me?

353
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,160
I know it's a big ask

354
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:24,120
but we've made up for half
of the money from the incident.

355
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:25,997
With this,
we should be able to get by.

356
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,957
Even so, how can you expect
a legal review

357
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,542
to be done in an hour?

358
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,045
You call it a legal review

359
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,296
but you're just asking
for instant approval.

360
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,049
We just can't miss
the window on this.

361
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:39,887
Then you should've brought
a normal contract.

362
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:41,388
I mean, what is this?

363
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:43,890
I've never even seen
or heard of such clauses.

364
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:44,975
Why are they included?

365
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:47,937
Well, I didn't write it.

366
00:19:51,232 --> 00:19:52,483
I get that you're in a rush

367
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,694
but we have procedures to follow
and an obligation of responsibility.

368
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:58,948
If we approve this contract,
we have to explain why.

369
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,740
Of course, I'm well aware of that.

370
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,075
I'm asking for a favor.

371
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:03,869
I'm not asking without knowing that.

372
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:09,208
Your whole team is unbelievable.

373
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,848
Are you from Hongsung?

374
00:21:06,182 --> 00:21:07,183
Yes.

375
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:11,479
Have a seat.

376
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:20,488
Thank you for coming all this way.

377
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:21,947
Not at all.

378
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:24,784
With the nice weather,
it felt like I was going on a picnic.

379
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,914
I see you have
a hobby in woodworking.

380
00:21:30,581 --> 00:21:33,459
Working in showbiz can feel
pretty pointless sometimes.

381
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:35,795
It all seems like an illusion.

382
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:38,798
Making something with my hands

383
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,759
feels like it's helping improve
my mental health.

384
00:21:43,052 --> 00:21:45,054
Besides, I don't have
any other hobbies.

385
00:21:46,222 --> 00:21:47,223
That's all.

386
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:49,433
It's nice to see this.

387
00:21:49,892 --> 00:21:52,603
Most people have hobbies
where they use things.

388
00:21:53,062 --> 00:21:54,563
But you're building things instead.

389
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:59,401
So what's the plan?

390
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:01,945
Oh, right.

391
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:04,697
I'm not good at small talk.

392
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,867
I gave it my best shot just now.

393
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:11,205
I doubt it's good news,
so just tell me and get it over with.

394
00:22:13,249 --> 00:22:15,209
Why do you think
it won't be good news?

395
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:19,964
Aren't you here to terminate
my modeling contract?

396
00:22:20,548 --> 00:22:21,965
You're launching a new brand.

397
00:22:21,966 --> 00:22:26,470
There's no need to use an actress
who's getting divorced as your model.

398
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:30,099
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you

399
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:32,393
before signing the contract.

400
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:35,563
Marriage can be a cycle

401
00:22:36,313 --> 00:22:38,524
of separation and reconciliation.

402
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:42,319
I didn't know
if we'd actually get divorced.

403
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:45,573
Besides, divorce isn't a flaw.

404
00:22:48,409 --> 00:22:49,952
We don't plan
to terminate the contract.

405
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,497
I just came here to ask you a favor.

406
00:22:55,583 --> 00:22:56,584
What is it?

407
00:22:58,544 --> 00:23:00,546
Sorry, I have to check this message.
It's important.

408
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:04,675
LEGAL REVIEW COMPLETE
YOU CAN GIVE HER THE CONTRACT

409
00:23:06,302 --> 00:23:07,303
My apologies.

410
00:23:11,015 --> 00:23:12,725
We'd like to sign a new contract.

411
00:23:14,310 --> 00:23:17,020
Please take a look
at the contract first.

412
00:23:17,021 --> 00:23:19,481
Paperwork gives me a headache
these days.

413
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:22,108
Can my lawyer look at it
and give you a call?

414
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:23,192
Sure.

415
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:26,155
In that case,
could you just check Article 8?

416
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:30,326
What's in Article 8?

417
00:23:30,576 --> 00:23:31,993
ARTICLE 8: MORALITY CLAUSE

418
00:23:31,994 --> 00:23:34,038
We revised the morality clause.

419
00:23:36,206 --> 00:23:37,498
As you can see

420
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:41,170
we've included a morality clause
for both parties.

421
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:46,342
The clause is usually included
in case of a model's controversy.

422
00:23:46,759 --> 00:23:50,095
But there are also many cases
of brand controversy harming models.

423
00:23:50,638 --> 00:23:53,349
However, since we're the employer

424
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:55,309
the penalty fee amount is different.

425
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:58,353
We'd appreciate your understanding
on that matter.

426
00:23:58,354 --> 00:24:00,773
You want to include
a bilateral morality clause?

427
00:24:03,233 --> 00:24:04,234
Is it even allowed?

428
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:07,154
Your divorce shouldn't be considered
a controversy.

429
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:11,157
If you're worried about
contract termination due to that

430
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:13,576
then I believe
the contract is unfair.

431
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:14,954
Thus, we revised the clause.

432
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:18,332
So I'll just ask you one question.

433
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:20,834
Were you at fault

434
00:24:22,211 --> 00:24:23,545
for your divorce?

435
00:24:27,675 --> 00:24:29,676
We were both at fault.

436
00:24:29,677 --> 00:24:32,554
However, to answer your question

437
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:35,099
I did nothing wrong.

438
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:38,476
That's all I needed to know.

439
00:24:38,477 --> 00:24:39,478
Let's sign the contract.

440
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:46,609
If you wanted to terminate,
I would have no excuses.

441
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:49,029
Instead, you came
with an even better contract.

442
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,991
So what would you like me to do?

443
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:55,160
Please attend your divorce hearing.

444
00:24:57,413 --> 00:24:59,373
I assume you want me
to wear Laknes's shoes?

445
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,083
Yes.

446
00:25:08,507 --> 00:25:09,717
You're something else.

447
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,593
I'm fully aware that it's a big ask.

448
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:14,513
Is that why you came
with the revised contract?

449
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:23,480
I'll do it.

450
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:28,485
I'm also aware of how difficult it is
to write a contract like this.

451
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:31,030
Thank you.

452
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:35,909
Mr. Gong.

453
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:38,537
Would you consider being my manager?

454
00:25:40,998 --> 00:25:42,290
I'm serious.

455
00:25:42,291 --> 00:25:43,709
I'll pay more
than your current salary.

456
00:25:47,296 --> 00:25:48,297
Will you consider it?

457
00:25:49,757 --> 00:25:50,758
No.

458
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,552
I was just thinking
of a polite way to say this.

459
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:55,262
Just say it.

460
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,222
I wasn't polite, either.

461
00:25:59,183 --> 00:26:00,184
I'm sorry

462
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:02,644
but I have money too.

463
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:09,651
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

464
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:54,214
WHAT A SIMPLE, YET ELEGANT LOOK

465
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:56,300
WALKING TO COURT LIKE IT'S A RUNWAY
#YOOJIHYUN

466
00:27:57,092 --> 00:27:58,301
WHAT BRAND ARE HER SHOES?

467
00:27:58,302 --> 00:27:59,427
THE NEW LINE FROM LAKNES

468
00:27:59,428 --> 00:28:00,511
I ALREADY GOT A PAIR

469
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:01,596
LAKNES NEW COLLECTION!

470
00:28:01,597 --> 00:28:02,722
THE PERFECT MONOTONE LOOK

471
00:28:02,723 --> 00:28:04,016
THE SHOES COMPLETE THE LOOK

472
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:06,726
SO PRETTY I'M SPEECHLESS
#YOOJIHYUN #GODDESS

473
00:28:06,727 --> 00:28:07,728
BOOKMARKING THIS
I WANT TO COPY HER LOOK

474
00:28:08,145 --> 00:28:11,439
CAN ANYONE TELL ME
WHERE HER SHOES ARE FROM?

475
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:13,317
LAKNES, I'M BUYING A PAIR TODAY

476
00:28:15,485 --> 00:28:16,986
BLACK MARY JANE PUMPS

477
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:18,488
ORDER COMPLETE

478
00:29:04,910 --> 00:29:06,119
TOTAL OFFLINE AND ONLINE SALES

479
00:29:07,871 --> 00:29:09,080
JULY: 3,893,858,858 WON
AUGUST: 4,337,122,530 WON

480
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:10,873
SALES INCREASE: 443,263,672
GROWTH RATE: 11%

481
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:12,209
SEPTEMBER,
SALES INCREASE, GROWTH RATE

482
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:22,176
I've never seen sales increase
by 1400% in a single month.

483
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:23,887
- Me neither.
- Same here.

484
00:29:24,263 --> 00:29:27,266
What if they made a mistake like me
and added an extra zero?

485
00:29:27,849 --> 00:29:28,934
You little...

486
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:30,435
I'll hit you too.

487
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:32,270
Join in, Ji-hye.

488
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:33,354
I'm okay.

489
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:35,022
Come on, you suffered a lot.

490
00:29:35,023 --> 00:29:36,274
Don't regret missing out later.

491
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:37,567
It's okay, Ji-hye. Hit me.

492
00:29:38,652 --> 00:29:40,027
- What do I do?
- What else?

493
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:41,697
Time to leave him alone
and get back to work.

494
00:29:42,406 --> 00:29:44,657
Please, Mr. Gong. I'm sorry.

495
00:29:44,658 --> 00:29:45,741
Shall we, Mr. Gong?

496
00:29:45,742 --> 00:29:46,826
- It's 1400%.
- You little...

497
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,035
Please.

498
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:49,329
- What are you doing?
- Seriously.

499
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,624
I'm sorry, sir.

500
00:29:53,375 --> 00:29:54,584
Come with me.

501
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:58,880
The vice president?

502
00:29:59,506 --> 00:30:00,632
Why, all of a sudden?

503
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:02,467
I don't know, either.

504
00:30:03,552 --> 00:30:06,513
All I did was report
the sales growth numbers.

505
00:30:06,847 --> 00:30:08,556
The director was summoned right away.

506
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:09,891
That was 30 minutes ago.

507
00:30:11,268 --> 00:30:12,894
Do you think he'll reprimand us?

508
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,232
It wouldn't be weird
if he reprimanded us

509
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:20,527
nor would it be weird
if he praised us.

510
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:22,738
What do you think he'll do?

511
00:30:23,322 --> 00:30:26,742
If he reprimands me,
I'll listen calmly.

512
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:29,870
And if he praises me,
I'll listen humbly.

513
00:30:31,621 --> 00:30:33,373
So you don't mind either way?

514
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:36,668
He's free to judge it
however he sees fit.

515
00:30:37,002 --> 00:30:38,587
If I went back in time

516
00:30:39,046 --> 00:30:41,088
I wouldn't do anything differently.

517
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:42,549
So it doesn't matter to me.

518
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:51,516
What is it?

519
00:30:54,186 --> 00:30:55,896
I've got a bad feeling about this.

520
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:08,784
Come in.

521
00:31:19,378 --> 00:31:20,420
Have a seat.

522
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,438
Mr. Gong.

523
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,441
Is it your first time here?

524
00:31:43,318 --> 00:31:44,694
Yes, sir.

525
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:46,988
Why do you think I called you?

526
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:50,783
I'm not sure, sir.

527
00:31:50,784 --> 00:31:52,035
You must have some idea.

528
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:58,833
Our sales increased significantly,
but it was due to a mistake.

529
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:00,877
So I came expecting a reprimand.

530
00:32:02,796 --> 00:32:03,922
I was curious.

531
00:32:06,091 --> 00:32:09,302
You successfully launched a brand
no one else wanted to take on.

532
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:12,472
We sent you to Italy
to cut out the traitor

533
00:32:13,056 --> 00:32:15,183
but you practically turned him
into our subsidiary instead.

534
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:17,644
You made a mistake with the order

535
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:19,270
but now it looks like
you had the foresight

536
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:20,897
to preorder
before the brand took off.

537
00:32:21,982 --> 00:32:23,775
That's enough to pique my curiosity.

538
00:32:24,818 --> 00:32:26,361
I've come up
with two possible conclusions.

539
00:32:27,571 --> 00:32:29,448
You're either overqualified
for the position

540
00:32:30,490 --> 00:32:31,950
or you're overstepping your role.

541
00:32:41,877 --> 00:32:43,044
Why don't you take this on?

542
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:49,342
Recently, we got a tip-off
about corruption in Sales Division 2.

543
00:32:50,177 --> 00:32:51,720
So we reprimanded them.

544
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:53,972
But not long after,
we got another tip-off.

545
00:32:54,848 --> 00:32:57,183
We found a cockroach in our house

546
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:59,977
so we quickly blocked the drains
and sprayed pesticide

547
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,480
but it was of no use.

548
00:33:02,731 --> 00:33:05,192
The house is already infested.

549
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,236
In the end,
the Audit Team decided to step up.

550
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:10,906
But they lack hands-on experience.

551
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:13,950
I'd like you to help them.

552
00:33:21,166 --> 00:33:22,167
Well...

553
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:24,753
With all due respect

554
00:33:26,463 --> 00:33:28,047
if another division
conducts the audit

555
00:33:28,048 --> 00:33:30,300
there will be a lot of pushback
from Division 2.

556
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:33,261
That's why I'm leaving it to you.

557
00:33:34,888 --> 00:33:35,889
Go make some noise.

558
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,731
Can you do a good job?

559
00:33:46,399 --> 00:33:47,734
I'll work hard.

560
00:33:48,527 --> 00:33:49,861
Work hard, of course.

561
00:33:50,362 --> 00:33:51,863
Doing a good job is a given.

562
00:33:53,657 --> 00:33:55,116
Watch your expression.

563
00:33:55,534 --> 00:33:57,368
There's nothing more annoying
than an auditor

564
00:33:57,369 --> 00:33:58,828
going around with a smile.

565
00:34:00,247 --> 00:34:01,248
Yes, ma'am.

566
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:04,960
I've got a bad feeling about this.

567
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:21,767
If another division
conducts the audit

568
00:34:21,768 --> 00:34:24,187
there will be a lot of pushback
from Division 2.

569
00:34:24,938 --> 00:34:26,898
That's why I'm leaving it to you.

570
00:34:27,482 --> 00:34:28,650
Go make some noise.

571
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:34,488
The branch was deeply corrupt.

572
00:34:34,489 --> 00:34:38,410
Word is, Jang Hyang-eun
was at the center of it all.

573
00:34:38,660 --> 00:34:40,829
I'm sure you have
many questions for me.

574
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:42,872
Why haven't you asked me anything?

575
00:35:06,396 --> 00:35:07,397
Over here.

576
00:35:14,696 --> 00:35:16,823
Why did you ask to meet outside?

577
00:35:18,617 --> 00:35:20,327
I wanted to speak with you privately.

578
00:35:20,994 --> 00:35:22,120
I'm nervous now.

579
00:35:22,621 --> 00:35:24,998
I doubt it. I know you're not
the type to get nervous.

580
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:27,876
Let me rephrase. I'm concerned.

581
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:30,920
Have a taste.
The coffee here is delicious.

582
00:35:37,636 --> 00:35:40,847
Ms. Jang, I want to ask you a favor.

583
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:42,223
Sure, what is it?

584
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:45,435
There will be an audit
of Sales Division 2 soon.

585
00:35:45,935 --> 00:35:48,772
I will be assisting them
on the ground.

586
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:52,317
A sales division is auditing
another sales division?

587
00:35:52,734 --> 00:35:53,901
That's right.

588
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:55,528
There will be a lot of backlash.

589
00:35:56,571 --> 00:35:57,864
You know that, right?

590
00:35:58,490 --> 00:35:59,491
Of course.

591
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:03,911
If it's okay with you,
I'd like you to join me.

592
00:36:03,912 --> 00:36:05,038
What do you say?

593
00:36:11,378 --> 00:36:14,964
You know, I like Gi-tae more now
after the incident.

594
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:17,466
Because he ran around
trying to fix it himself?

595
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:20,345
Yes, he did all he could
to solve it on his own.

596
00:36:20,804 --> 00:36:21,805
I'm the same way.

597
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,683
So it was nice to see him do that.

598
00:36:25,558 --> 00:36:26,975
Yes, it was impressive.

599
00:36:26,976 --> 00:36:27,977
However...

600
00:36:29,437 --> 00:36:31,188
Once I became a team leader

601
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:33,775
I was assigned tasks
I couldn't complete on my own.

602
00:36:34,150 --> 00:36:37,696
I confidently said
I'd take the Laknes project

603
00:36:38,071 --> 00:36:39,906
but Mr. Yang is the one
who actually resolved things.

604
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:43,368
I can't complete this task
on my own, either.

605
00:36:44,452 --> 00:36:45,578
I need your help, Ms. Jang.

606
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:50,709
Mr. Gong.

607
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:54,713
Why do you think
I came back from China?

608
00:36:55,797 --> 00:36:58,215
Don't you think
I was involved in the corruption?

609
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:00,427
I don't think
you were completely uninvolved.

610
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:04,556
Then how can I join the Audit Team?

611
00:37:07,517 --> 00:37:09,144
Were you involved in corruption?

612
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:16,401
I guess you signed
a non-disclosure agreement.

613
00:37:17,402 --> 00:37:19,154
In that case, just listen.

614
00:37:20,488 --> 00:37:21,905
In my opinion

615
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:23,575
I don't think
you committed corruption.

616
00:37:24,576 --> 00:37:26,745
But you're involved in it somehow.

617
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,539
Whether by choice or circumstance,
you might've played a role.

618
00:37:30,123 --> 00:37:31,916
I think you're staying silent

619
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:34,335
out of courtesy to your colleagues.

620
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:38,423
So this is my conclusion.

621
00:37:40,049 --> 00:37:41,593
You're the whistleblower, aren't you?

622
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:52,061
I know that reporting your colleague
weighs on you.

623
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:55,731
I've also dared to imagine
the things you endured

624
00:37:55,732 --> 00:37:57,192
after blowing the whistle.

625
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:01,570
You had to stay silent
in the face of everyone's whispers.

626
00:38:01,571 --> 00:38:04,491
And you had no way
to explain yourself.

627
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:10,163
Let people talk if they want to.

628
00:38:11,372 --> 00:38:14,083
How about we just do
what is in our power?

629
00:38:17,921 --> 00:38:19,422
Do this with me.

630
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:22,467
I'll help you carry the weight
on your shoulders.

631
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:26,596
Are you asking me
to help me feel better?

632
00:38:27,013 --> 00:38:29,432
Well, it's not just that.

633
00:38:30,683 --> 00:38:32,435
They say it takes one to know one.

634
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:36,105
I thought you'd be well-versed
since you have experience with this.

635
00:38:42,362 --> 00:38:47,283
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

636
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:04,676
2 MONTHS AGO, CHINA

637
00:39:12,809 --> 00:39:13,852
Have you made up your mind?

638
00:39:14,644 --> 00:39:15,645
Yes.

639
00:39:25,989 --> 00:39:27,115
Do you know

640
00:39:28,575 --> 00:39:31,870
what being a whistleblower entails?

641
00:39:32,662 --> 00:39:34,246
I'm well aware.

642
00:39:34,247 --> 00:39:35,248
No.

643
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:36,875
You have no clue.

644
00:39:37,750 --> 00:39:40,336
For starters,
you must have a spotless record.

645
00:39:41,004 --> 00:39:44,549
Not just professionally, but in life.

646
00:39:45,049 --> 00:39:47,551
Even something as minor as littering

647
00:39:47,552 --> 00:39:50,638
will be used to criticize you
and say you're no better.

648
00:39:51,431 --> 00:39:54,809
But sure, let's say
you've never littered even once.

649
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:58,438
Do you think people
will call you a hero?

650
00:39:58,897 --> 00:39:59,898
No way.

651
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:01,774
No matter the reason

652
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:05,652
it's instinctual to avoid someone
who betrays their colleague.

653
00:40:05,653 --> 00:40:08,781
Even more so in a small,
crowded country like Korea!

654
00:40:09,866 --> 00:40:11,034
Moving forward

655
00:40:11,284 --> 00:40:14,370
no one will want to work with you.

656
00:40:15,079 --> 00:40:16,372
Just know that.

657
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:20,792
Be honest with me.

658
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:23,421
Did you really not know
what we were doing?

659
00:40:23,963 --> 00:40:25,923
Come on. You knew, didn't you?

660
00:40:25,924 --> 00:40:27,425
A clever girl like you?

661
00:40:27,884 --> 00:40:29,968
You just looked the other way.

662
00:40:29,969 --> 00:40:32,679
So we gave you luxury stuff
to keep looking the other way!

663
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:36,433
You knew we used company funds
to hire your housekeeper.

664
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:38,352
Yes, I knew everything.

665
00:40:38,353 --> 00:40:39,395
Come on!

666
00:40:42,649 --> 00:40:43,650
Then why?

667
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:46,235
Why are you doing this?

668
00:40:48,363 --> 00:40:50,281
Do you mind if I have a smoke?

669
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:51,866
What?

670
00:40:52,784 --> 00:40:53,993
I'm getting angry.

671
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,551
Do you know why I'm angry?

672
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:14,138
You used the company's work
for personal profit.

673
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:17,183
You're even blatantly
embezzling company funds.

674
00:41:18,518 --> 00:41:21,437
And now you're asking me
why I want to come forward?

675
00:41:22,689 --> 00:41:23,773
Are you kidding me?

676
00:41:24,649 --> 00:41:26,442
Of course, I'm not perfect, either.

677
00:41:27,110 --> 00:41:28,611
Sure, I've littered before.

678
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:32,949
And as you said, I caught on
that you were using company funds

679
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:34,701
to butter me up.

680
00:41:35,368 --> 00:41:37,328
So I tried to let it slide.

681
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:39,497
But I just couldn't.

682
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,417
The longer this goes on,
the more I'll struggle.

683
00:41:45,378 --> 00:41:47,130
Why do you work, sir?

684
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:49,632
As for me

685
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:52,719
I've done nothing but work
since I grew up.

686
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:56,097
I have no hobbies.
I don't even work out.

687
00:41:56,848 --> 00:41:57,849
But...

688
00:41:59,183 --> 00:42:00,768
If the work is lousy

689
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:03,438
that also makes me lousy.

690
00:42:06,691 --> 00:42:07,941
That's why I'm doing this.

691
00:42:07,942 --> 00:42:09,193
I don't want to be lousy.

692
00:42:12,739 --> 00:42:13,906
I need to quit smoking.

693
00:44:46,184 --> 00:44:48,144
Subtitles by Eunice Kim
